WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:02.673
(soft string music)

00:00:02.673 --> 00:00:04.305
- [Voiceover] What I love
about seeing bats is just

00:00:04.305 --> 00:00:06.300
how graceful they are.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.871
The way they fly, they flip,
they flutter, they move.

00:00:08.871 --> 00:00:11.396
- It's moving out now.

00:00:11.396 --> 00:00:13.721
- [Voiceover] They're just stunning.

00:00:13.721 --> 00:00:16.129
It was just kind of a love
at first sight that has

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:18.614
stayed with me my entire life.

00:00:18.614 --> 00:00:21.114
They're just part of my world.

00:00:22.165 --> 00:00:24.998
(bats fluttering)

00:00:32.646 --> 00:00:35.671
I am Kirsten Alvey-Mudd,
the Executive Director

00:00:35.671 --> 00:00:38.588
and founder of Missouri Bat Census.

00:00:39.684 --> 00:00:41.474
- And I'm a bat lady.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.891
(quick percussion music)

00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:50.169
- [Voiceover] When we
heard word in 2006 about

00:00:50.169 --> 00:00:54.336
white nose syndrome I knew that
we had a very short window.

00:00:55.282 --> 00:00:57.486
White nose syndrome is a fungus

00:00:57.486 --> 00:01:00.472
that grows on a bat's nose,
on its wings, on its tail,

00:01:00.472 --> 00:01:03.371
anywhere where the bat doesn't have fur.

00:01:03.371 --> 00:01:05.003
It causes it to wake too many times

00:01:05.003 --> 00:01:07.836
from its winter hibernation sleep.

00:01:09.122 --> 00:01:11.238
They may hang where they're
at in a cave and just

00:01:11.238 --> 00:01:14.870
starve to death or fly
out on a cold day and will

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.953
be lost on the landscape.

00:01:18.013 --> 00:01:19.601
- See these little blotches in his wing?

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.192
That's what we're looking for.

00:01:21.192 --> 00:01:23.521
- [Voiceover] It also
invades a bat's wings tissue

00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:26.782
and it eats away at their wings.

00:01:26.782 --> 00:01:28.209
- Hey, but it's almost spring, buddy.

00:01:28.209 --> 00:01:29.598
You got a chance to make it.

00:01:29.598 --> 00:01:32.681
Some of your roomies did not survive.

00:01:33.802 --> 00:01:35.352
See how we have a dead bat here.

00:01:35.352 --> 00:01:36.903
Another bat right there.

00:01:36.903 --> 00:01:39.474
Another good-sized one there.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:41.677
It's really hard, not just
because I enjoy the caving

00:01:41.677 --> 00:01:43.432
but I enjoy the bats themselves.

00:01:43.432 --> 00:01:45.226
And I just want to do
everything to protect them

00:01:45.226 --> 00:01:47.875
and help them hang on
until we find some method

00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:51.042
that we can intervene on their behalf.

00:01:52.644 --> 00:01:54.584
(upbeat enthusiastic music)

00:01:54.584 --> 00:01:56.820
- [Voiceover] We’ve began our
bat rescue and rehab programs

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.369
here in the State of Missouri.

00:01:58.369 --> 00:02:00.365
- Are you hungry?

00:02:00.365 --> 00:02:02.689
- [Voiceover] Right now, the
bats that I have at my location

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.160
are all big brown bats.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.367
These guys all came into
us as little orphaned

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:07.534
hairless pups.

00:02:08.529 --> 00:02:10.565
In the next few weeks they'll
be getting a chance to see

00:02:10.565 --> 00:02:12.318
if they can fly and eat
and maintain their weight

00:02:12.318 --> 00:02:14.033
on their own, in the
hopes of releasing them

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.626
back into the wild.

00:02:15.626 --> 00:02:17.876
- Are you looking for more?

00:02:19.923 --> 00:02:23.504
There are so many
misconceptions about bats.

00:02:23.504 --> 00:02:26.136
I just wish that everybody
would realize that they have

00:02:26.136 --> 00:02:29.563
an integral part of our ecosystem.

00:02:29.563 --> 00:02:31.523
There's a real sense of
pride that we have helped

00:02:31.523 --> 00:02:35.522
these bats gain in population numbers.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.076
Nobody has to pat me on the back for it.

00:02:37.076 --> 00:02:40.011
I feel it, it's the thank
you from them as I see

00:02:40.011 --> 00:02:42.459
many more and more of
them surviving and living

00:02:42.459 --> 00:02:44.418
healthy and happy.

00:02:44.418 --> 00:02:46.234
That's what I'm out for.

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:49.734
(energetic string music)

